From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <aaronhritz@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:08:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pdu): keep license keying material and licenses out of
 Debug output

The licensing PDUs derived Debug, so a log at the debug or trace level
printed the premaster secret, the MAC salt and license keys, the client
and server randoms, the encrypted HWID, the platform challenge and its
response, and the license itself, as the server sent it, byte by byte;
also the user and machine names the client announces. Such a log can't
be handed to anyone.

Those fields now print as their length only (`<48 bytes withheld>`), in
Debug implementations of their own, and so does the server certificate's
material (chain, modulus, signature). What tells an exchange apart stays:
the security and license headers (message type, flags, version, size),
the product and scope, error codes and state transitions. The connector
also logs the Server License Request and the error message that ends an
exchange without one at the debug level, as it already did the later
PDUs, so that a debug log shows the whole exchange.
---
